  "worked_solution": "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=7,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(y-{y}_{1})^{2} & =(-2){(y-7)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2){(y-7)}^{2} & =(-2)({y}^{2}-14y+49) \\\\  & =-2{y}^{2}+28y-98.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(y)=-2{y}^{2}+28y-98.$",
